<h1>webshell</h1>
<p class="prompt">a guest session on this node. it boots, it auto-logs-in, and
  it drops you at a prompt — all of it in your browser, none of it on a server.
  the filesystem is a JavaScript object; read <code>/js/webshell.js</code> and
  you've read the whole machine.</p>

<div class="shell" id="shell">
  <div id="shell-output"></div>
  <form class="shell-input-line" id="shell-form" hidden>
    <label class="visually-hidden" for="shell-input">shell command</label>
    <span class="shell-prompt" id="shell-prompt">guest@sp3ctr-zone:~$</span>
    <input class="shell-input" id="shell-input" type="text" autocomplete="off"
           autocapitalize="off" autocorrect="off" spellcheck="false">
  </form>
</div>

<p class="note">the session is confined to <code>/home/guest</code>, the way a
  chroot would confine it — anything resolving outside that gets
  <code>ACCESS_DENIED</code>. nothing is written, nothing is stored, and
  nothing leaves the page. start with <code>help</code>.</p>
